    "okro": "Okro",
    "okro_economic_value": "The vegetable is rich in vitamins and minerals, making it a valuable component in diets around the world,okra has industrial applications, including use in processed foods and as a thickening agent in various products.",
    "okro_local_value": "It is a staple vegetable in local diets, contributing to food diversity and nutrition,a key ingredient in traditional dishes such as gumbo and soups, okra supports local economies through its cultivation and sale in markets. ",
    "okro_desc": "Okra plants are typically bushy and can grow up to 6 feet (1.8 meters) tall. They have large, broad, lobed leaves that are usually dark green. The plant produces tall, slender, and upright stems with beautiful, hibiscus-like flowers that are often yellow or white with a red or purple center. When okra is ready to harvest, the seed pods are green, elongated, and covered in small, soft hairs. The pods are about 3 to 6 inches (7.5 to 15 cm) long and are harvested while they are still tender. They have a slightly ridged surface and contain small, edible seeds. Okra should be picked before it becomes too mature and tough.",
    "okro_habitat": "Òjò gbòòrò: Ilá fẹ́ràn ibi tí ó gbona, tí ó sì ní òjò gbòòrò. Ó dára jùlọ nígbà tí ìgbà òtútù kò sí. Òjò tó dara fún Ilá ní láàrin 75°F àti 95°F (24°C sí 35°C).Aìkọ̀tútù: Ilá kì í fẹ́ ibi tí òtútù máa ń wà. Ilá máa ń gbòòrò nínú ibi tí ìgbà gbígbóná rẹ̀ pẹ́.Ìmọ̀lẹ̀ òrùn púpọ̀: Ilá fẹ́ràn ìmọ̀lẹ̀ òrùn fún wakati mẹ̀fà sí mẹ̀jọ (6-8) ní ọjọ́ kan. Ìmọ̀lẹ̀ òrùn tí ó tó kì í ṣe pàtàkì fún igbó àwọn àtẹgùn Ilá.",
   
    "african_spinach":"African Spinach",
    "africa_spinach_desc":"African Spinach is a leafy green vegetable that is highly valued in West African cuisine. It has broad, tender leaves that can vary in color from green to reddish-purple, depending on the species. The plant is fast-growing and can reach heights of up to 1 meter.",
    "africa_spinach_eco":" African Spinach is a staple in many Yoruba dishes, including Ẹ̀fọ́ rírò, where it is used to add a rich, earthy flavor and nutritional content. It is also popular in salads, soups, and as a side dish. The leaves are rich in vitamins, minerals, and antioxidants, making them beneficial for overall health",
