"yam": "Yam",
"yam_desc":"Yam  is a tuberous root vegetable that is a staple food in many West African communities. The plant has large, heart-shaped leaves and underground tubers that can grow to significant sizes. Yam plants can grow up to 3 meters in length and typically produce tubers after several months of growth.",
"yam_eco":"yam is rich in carbohydrates, vitamins, and dietary fiber, providing essential energy and nutrients.",
"yam_local":"yam holds great significance in Yoruba society, symbolizing prosperity, fertility, and social status. It is often used in rituals and as offerings during religious ceremonies.",
"yam_habit":"Yam is predominantly grown in well-drained, fertile soils, with the best yields during the rainy season, making it a vital crop for both subsistence and economic trade in the region.",
